---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const compose = `services:
  actual:
    image: actualbudget/actual-server:latest
    restart: unless-stopped
    volumes:
      - ./actual-data:/data

  abt:
    image: ghcr.io/aelxxs/abt-sidecar:latest
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      ACTUAL_ORIGIN: http://actual:5006
    ports:
      - "3005:3005"
    depends_on:
      - actual`;
---

<Base
	title="Self-hosting — Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="Run Actual Budget Tweaks as a sidecar next to your Actual server, so every browser gets it without installing the extension."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/" class="docs__back">&larr; Back to home</a>
			<h1>Self-hosting</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				The sidecar is a small proxy that sits in front of your Actual server and adds Actual Budget
				Tweaks to every browser that opens it. No extension needed.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Extension or sidecar?</h2>
			<div class="docs__table-wrap">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th></th><th>Extension</th><th>Sidecar</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td>Install</td><td>Once per browser</td><td>Once per server</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Works in</td><td>Chrome and Firefox</td><td>Any browser that opens your Actual address</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Updates</td><td>Automatic, through the browser</td><td>When you pull a new image</td></tr>
						<tr><td>Settings</td><td>Synced with each budget</td><td>Synced with each budget</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				Use one or the other for a given Actual address. If the extension is pointed at the same
				address as the sidecar, Actual Budget Tweaks loads twice.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Quick start</h2>
			<p>Add the sidecar next to Actual in your <code>docker-compose.yml</code>:</p>
			<pre><code>{compose}</code></pre>
			<p>
				Start it with <code>docker compose up -d</code>, then open <code>http://your-server:3005</code>.
				The image runs on both <code>amd64</code> and <code>arm64</code>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Adding it to an existing setup</h2>
			<ol>
				<li>Add the <code>abt</code> service above, with <code>ACTUAL_ORIGIN</code> set to the address your Actual container answers on.</li>
				<li>Point your reverse proxy (Caddy, nginx, Traefik…) at <code>abt:3005</code> instead of <code>actual:5006</code>.</li>
				<li>Stop publishing Actual's own port, so the sidecar is the only way in.</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				Your login, budgets and server settings are untouched. The sidecar only changes the page
				Actual sends to the browser.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Configuration</h2>
			<div class="docs__table-wrap">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td><code>ACTUAL_ORIGIN</code></td><td><code>http://actual:5006</code></td><td>Where the sidecar reaches your Actual server</td></tr>
						<tr><td><code>PORT</code></td><td><code>3005</code></td><td>Port the sidecar listens on inside the container</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Updating</h2>
			<p>
				<code>latest</code> follows every release. Update with
				<code>docker compose pull &amp;&amp; docker compose up -d</code>. To stay on a release, use its
				version tag instead, for example <code>ghcr.io/aelxxs/abt-sidecar:0.1.75</code>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Where your settings live</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Tweaks settings are saved in the budget itself, through Actual's synced preferences, so they follow it to every device and browser that opens it. Switching between the extension and the sidecar keeps them.</li>
				<li>Each budget has its own settings. A budget opened for the first time starts from the settings this browser already has.</li>
				<li>Changes from another device apply when you come back to the tab. A few settings ask you to reload.</li>
				<li>Each browser keeps a copy to load from. Clearing site data only clears that copy; the budget's settings come back the next time you open it.</li>
				<li>Local-only budgets, not synced to a server, keep their settings on that device.</li>
				<li>The sidecar stores nothing. Your budget data stays in Actual.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Security</h2>
			<p>What the sidecar does to the traffic passing through it:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Adds the Tweaks scripts and styles to Actual's page. Every other request and response passes through unchanged.</li>
				<li>
					Sends a Content-Security-Policy that only runs scripts from your own server, and only allows
					connections to the services Tweaks uses: Yahoo Finance (stock widgets), GitHub (community
					themes, release notes and Actual's own update check), and exchangerate-api.com (currency conversion).
				</li>
				<li>Adds the real client address to <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>, so Actual's login rate limit still applies per visitor.</li>
				<li>Relays stock price lookups to Yahoo Finance, which doesn't allow direct browser requests. Only requests from your own Actual page are accepted, and the symbol and parameters are validated.</li>
				<li>Runs as an unprivileged user inside the container.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Recommended:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Serve it over HTTPS through your reverse proxy.</li>
				<li>Don't expose Actual's port directly.</li>
				<li>
					If you've set <code>ACTUAL_TRUSTED_PROXIES</code> on Actual, include the sidecar's Docker
					network. Otherwise Actual sees every visitor as the sidecar's address, and one person's failed
					logins can rate-limit everyone.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
			<dl class="docs__faq">
				<dt>Tweaks doesn't appear</dt>
				<dd>
					Make sure you're opening the sidecar's address, not Actual's. Opening
					<code>/abt/browser-shim.js</code> on that address should return a script.
				</dd>
				<dt>Features show up twice</dt>
				<dd>The extension is also pointed at this address. Remove the address from the extension, or disable it.</dd>
				<dt>Actual won't load inside another page</dt>
				<dd>The sidecar blocks embedding on other sites (for example a dashboard iframe), to prevent clickjacking.</dd>
				<dt>An Actual feature can't reach an outside service</dt>
				<dd>
					The security policy only allows the services listed above. Please
					<a href="https://github.com/aelxxs/actual-budget-tweaks/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue</a>
					with the feature and the blocked address shown in the browser console.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>

